    ("nutrition", "nutrition_question",
     ["Is intermittent fasting good for weight loss?", "Should I try intermittent fasting?"],
     "Intermittent fasting can help some people eat fewer calories, but research generally shows similar weight loss to other approaches with the same calorie deficit. It can be a useful structure if it suits your schedule. It's not recommended for people with a history of eating disorders, during pregnancy, or for some people with diabetes - check with a doctor first in those cases."),
